---
interface Props {
  kind:
    | 'cover'
    | 'question'
    | 'statistic'
    | 'chart'
    | 'recommendation'
    | 'challenge'
    | 'principle'
    | 'process'
    | 'case-study'
    | 'publication'
    | 'closing'
    | 'interlude'
    | 'evidence-field';
  ratio?: 'square' | 'portrait' | 'vertical';
}

const { kind, ratio = 'square' } = Astro.props;
const darkKinds = new Set(['cover', 'question', 'recommendation', 'principle', 'publication', 'interlude']);
const dark = darkKinds.has(kind);
const topic = ['question', 'recommendation'].includes(kind)
  ? 'Operating model'
  : ['cover', 'principle', 'challenge', 'closing', 'evidence-field'].includes(kind)
    ? 'Decision quality'
    : kind === 'case-study'
      ? 'Transformation'
      : 'Cost management';
---

<article class:list={['gs-frame', `gs-frame--${kind}`, `gs-frame--${ratio}`, { 'gs-frame--dark': dark }]}>
  <header class="gs-frame-head">
    <img src={dark ? '/assets/logo-lockup-forest.svg' : '/assets/logo-lockup-light.svg'} alt="GreenSquare AI" />
    <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{topic}</span>
  </header>

  {kind === 'cover' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-aperture" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <h3>Cut the review,<br />not the evidence</h3>
        <p>Where decision cost actually sits, in six frames.</p>
      </div>
      <footer><span>A six-part series on review cost</span><span>1 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'question' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-planes" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <small>Governing question</small>
        <h3>Which parts of our review cycle actually change the decision?</h3>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Owner: Chief Operating Officer</span><span>2 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'statistic' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <div class="gs-stat"><strong>9.3</strong><span>days</span></div>
        <p>Median time spent reworking a decision paper after internal challenge. It is the second-largest cost in the cycle and nobody owns it.</p>
        <b class="gs-state-label">Confirmed · 34 decisions</b>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Source: internal decision log, Jan–Jun 2026</span><span>3 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'chart' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <h3>Where the review cycle spends its time</h3>
        <small>Working days, median of 34 decisions</small>
        <div class="gs-mini-chart" role="img" aria-label="Evidence gathering 11.5 days, rework after challenge 9.3, internal challenge 7.4, sign-off 2.8">
          <div><span>Evidence gathering</span><i style="--value: 92%"></i><b>11.5</b></div>
          <div><span>Rework after challenge</span><i class="is-comparison" style="--value: 74%"></i><b>9.3</b></div>
          <div><span>Internal challenge</span><i style="--value: 59%"></i><b>7.4</b></div>
          <div><span>Sign-off</span><i style="--value: 22%"></i><b>2.8</b></div>
        </div>
        <p class="gs-chart-reading"><strong>What it means.</strong> Rework is the only stage without an owner, which is why it grows.</p>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Source: internal decision log, Jan–Jun 2026</span><span>4 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'recommendation' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <small>Recommendation</small>
        <h3>Give rework an owner before adding another review gate.</h3>
        <dl class="gs-decision-table">
          <div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>Chief Operating Officer</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Review date</dt><dd>30 November 2026</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Reverses if</dt><dd>Rework falls below four days without an owner</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Decision D/26.08/014</span><span>5 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'challenge' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <small>The challenge to this view</small>
        <h3>Most transformation programmes do not fail on execution. They fail because nobody wrote down what would change the recommendation.</h3>
        <p class="gs-challenge-line"><strong>What would change our mind.</strong> Two of the four sites report rework falling without a named owner.</p>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Source: site operations review, July 2026</span><span>Single post</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'principle' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-glass-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <h3>A recommendation you cannot reverse is not a recommendation. It is a preference with a deck attached.</h3>
        <p>Working principle, three of nine</p>
      </div>
      <footer><span>GreenSquare AI working principles</span><span>Single post</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'process' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <h3>How a decision earns its sign-off</h3>
        <ol class="gs-process">
          <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Question stated</strong><p>One governing question, in writing, with an owner.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Assumptions named</strong><p>Each one gets a test and a date, or it is dropped.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Challenge run</strong><p>Someone argues the other side on the same evidence.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Call made, with a reversal</strong><p>Owner, date, and what would reopen it.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <footer><span>The reversal returns the call to step two</span><span>Single post</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'case-study' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body gs-case-copy">
        <small>Proof point</small>
        <h3>Rework fell from 9.3 days to 3.1 once a single owner was named.</h3>
        <p>Four sites, one quarter, no change to the review gates.</p>
        <b class="gs-state-label">Confirmed · four sites</b>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-material-field" aria-label="Reserved half-bleed material or architectural photography field"><span>Material or architectural crop</span></div>
      <footer><span>Source: site operations review, July 2026</span><span></span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'publication' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-publication-mark" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <small>New paper</small>
        <h3>The cost of a decision nobody owns</h3>
        <p>Twelve pages on where review time goes, with the model behind it.</p>
        <span class="gs-frame-link">Read the paper</span>
      </div>
      <footer><span>August 2026</span><span>Single post</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'closing' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <h3>Name an owner for rework this quarter.</h3>
        <span class="gs-frame-link">Start with the free Decision Frame</span>
      </div>
      <footer><span>greensquare.ai</span><span>6 of 6</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'interlude' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-edge-light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="gs-frame-body"><h3>Nothing in the cycle is free. Somebody is already paying for the rework.</h3></div>
      <footer><span>Part of a six-frame series</span><span>Interlude</span></footer>
    </>
  )}

  {kind === 'evidence-field' && (
    <>
      <div class="gs-frame-body">
        <small>Evidence behind the call</small>
        <h3>34 confirmed. 9 assumptions. 7 open.</h3>
        <div class="gs-evidence-field" role="img" aria-label="A monochrome evidence field moving from dispersed claims to aligned claims across a stated threshold">
          {Array.from({ length: 30 }, (_, index) => <i class:list={[{ 'is-aligned': index > 18, 'is-small': index % 7 === 0 }]}></i>)}
          <span>Threshold: three sources agree</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <footer><span>Generated from the actual claim count</span><span>Single post</span></footer>
    </>
  )}
</article>
